Parity unit : page:charging/SmartCharge   kind=page   web route=/charging/schedule (+ /smart-charge)
Web source  : web/src/features/charging/pages/SmartChargePage.tsx (+ components/RateTimeline.tsx)
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/SmartChargePage/{SmartChargePage.Model.cs,
              SmartChargePage.Source.cs, SmartChargePage.ViewModel.cs, SmartChargePage.cs}  (real in-repo convention; see APPROACH)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feeds), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling
  W7 EnergyPage / BatteryDegradationPage / ApiLogsPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Charging/SmartChargePage.xaml + SmartChargePageViewModel.cs" is mapped onto
  these real conventions (no drift hidden — this note is the disclosure). The view-model is a manual
  INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable holder (not CommunityToolkit ObservableObject) because the headless test
  project (TeslaSync.App.Tests, plain net10.0) Compile-links the Model/Source/ViewModel and references only
  Generated + Core — matching the EnergyPage sibling exactly.
- The surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name "SmartCharge"
  (RouteTable.cs L259/L260 map both /smart-charge and the hidden /charging/schedule to name "SmartCharge")
  via ShellWindow.xaml.cs:
    _viewModel.PageFactory.Register("SmartCharge", static () => new FeatureViews.Charging.SmartChargePage());
  Namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Charging.
- PRE-EXISTING BUILD BREAKAGE REPAIRED (honesty, disclosure): at HEAD 184d28f1e the bare
  `dotnet build apps/windows/TeslaSync.sln -c Release` FAILED with 84 errors. Root cause: two unclosed
  PageFactory.Register lambdas in Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs ("YearReview" and "AutomationList") were missing
  their `return page; });` closers (a merge corruption), leaving the constructor braces unbalanced → CS1026/
  CS1002/CS1513 at the ctor close → the WinUI XAML compiler then cascaded into 80+ "unknown type" WMC0001/
  WMC0110 errors and a WMC9999 internal crash. The two lambdas were repaired (the file IS the allowed
  "NavigationView registration" target, and a green build is a gate precondition). No other behavior touched.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest's four web hooks are ported as four single-responsibility ports bound
  through the view-model (P1/S8), keeping the web hook names at the C# call sites:
    * useRatePlans       -> IRatePlansSource / RatePlansClientSource
                           GET  /charge-planner/rate-plans   (op get_api_v1_charge_planner_rate_plans)
    * useChargePlans     -> IChargePlansSource / ChargePlansClientSource
                           GET  /charge-planner/history?vehicle_id (op get_api_v1_charge_planner_history),
                           snake_case query (ADR-004 #8, no camelCase), scoped to the primary vehicle via the
                           shared IWidgetVehicleSource (native useSelectedVehicle; no vehicle => RepositoryResult.Empty,
                           web `enabled: !!vehicleId`).
    * useOptimizeCharge  -> IOptimizeChargeClient / OptimizeChargeClient
                           POST /charge-planner/optimize     (op post_api_v1_charge_planner_optimize)
    * useApplySchedule   -> IApplyScheduleClient / ApplyScheduleClient
                           POST /charge-planner/apply        (op post_api_v1_charge_planner_apply)
  The generated endpoint table types these four bodies as JsonElement, so feature-local DTOs are deserialized
  via IApiClient.SendAsync<T> (the contract client); the POST bodies are built as snake_case dictionaries
  (vehicle_id, target_soc, depart_by, rate_plan_id, max_amps, battery_capacity_kwh / plan_id) so the wire shape
  matches the Go handler regardless of the JsonSerializerDefaults.Web naming policy. No HTTP touches the view.
- States (ADR-006): the plan-history read is the page spine. SmartChargeState.Loading -> History TsTableSkeleton;
  Error -> History TsQueryError + Retry -> RefreshAsync; Empty -> History TsEmptyState (chargePlanner.noHistory);
  Ready -> History TsDataTable. The settings form, rate timeline, the three cost tiles and the schedule panel are
  ALWAYS rendered and NEVER collapse: before an optimization the cost tiles show em dashes, the schedule details
  show em dashes (Apply disabled), and the rate timeline shows its empty body (chargePlanner.noRateData). The
  optimize/apply mutations surface their own pending (TsButton.IsLoading) and error (ErrorText) states.
- SI / units: this planner endpoint's contract is dimensioned (cents/kWh, kWh, hours, %) exactly as the web page;
  costs are formatted at the display boundary via ScalarFormatters.FormatCurrency, percentages via
  FormatPercentage, plain numbers via FormatNumber, times/dates via DateTimeFormatting — never recomputed.
- Live data: none of the four charge-planner sources is an SSE stream, so no live subscription is created; the
  >2-minute staleness contract (ADR-013) is surfaced for the cached plan-history read via the header
  TsDataFreshness chip (UpdatedAt / IsFetching / IsError + the 2-minute CacheFreshness window).
- a11y/dark mode (ADR-015): every panel, the rate-timeline bars, the cost tiles, the history table, the schedule
  detail cells and the alternative rows publish AutomationProperties names; the design-token components
  (TsGlassPanel/Typography/TsStatCard/TsDataTable/TsButton/TsSelect/TsSlider) honor light/dark + high contrast via
  the W1/W2 token dictionaries; the page exposes its document title as its AutomationProperties name.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal flows through ILocalizer.GetString("chargePlanner.<key>", "<web default>")
  with the exact web key names; 32 of the 33 required keys were already in the platform catalog as
  translation.chargePlanner.* ; the one missing key (chargePlanner.cost_decimal — the web history "Cost" column key,
  distinct from the existing chargePlanner.cost) was appended to Strings/en|ar|he/Resources.resw (xml re-validated).

